摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Right-side file panel for DeepSeek Harness — auto-popup when the agent creates or downloads files, with image/text preview, reveal-in-folder and open actions. Bilingual · MIT","id":"gh:1334442899","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-file-panel","slug":"yu2025-luo/dsh-file-panel","topics":["cordis","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","file-preview","plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Right-side file panel for DeepSeek Harness — auto-popup when the agent creates or downloads files, w"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ith image/text preview, reveal-in-folder and open actions. Bilingual · MIT"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-file-panel"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"[](https://github.com/yu2025-luo/dsh-file-panel/actions/workflows/ci.yml) [](LICENSE)"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A plugin for DeepSeek Harness (`dsh` web GUI) that watches what the agent creates and downloads duri"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"ng a session, and shows it in a **right-side popup panel** — like the file viewer in Codex."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"When a file or image is written to disk during a session, the panel pops up automatically on the rig"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ht. Every row lets you:"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"- 👁 **Preview** — images render inline; text files show their first 256 KB; other types show metadat"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"a.\n- 📂 **Show in folder** — opens the OS file manager with the file selected (`explorer.exe /select`"},{"id":"p6s3","text":" on Windows, `open -R` on macOS, `xdg-open` on Linux).\n- ↗ **Open** — opens the file with the OS def"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"ault application (via the harness's built-in `host.openPath` RPC).\n- 📋 **Copy path** — copies the ab"},{"id":"p6s5","text":"solute path to the clipboard."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Also ships a **workspace folder** shortcut at the bottom of the panel."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"中文说明"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Screenshots"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"*The right-docked session files panel: every row previews, opens, reveals, or copies its path; the b"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ottom button opens the session's working directory. The panel is fully draggable (grab the header) a"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"nd resizable from its left and bottom edges, with scrollbars appearing when it gets narrow.*"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Requires DeepSeek Harness `dsh` CLI (npm package `@deepseek-ai/dsh`) and pnpm."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### From a local checkout"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### From GitHub"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The built artifacts are committed, so no build step runs during install."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### Activate"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Restart the `dsh web` server (plugin sets take effect on restart), then refresh\n`http://127.0.0.1:30"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"80`. That's it — no configuration required."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Remove with:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Usage"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"| Gesture | Result |"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"| Agent creates/downloads a file | Panel pops up automatically (newest files carry a `NEW` chip) |\n|"},{"id":"p24s2","text":" Click a row | Inline preview (image / text / metadata) |\n| Row hover actions | Preview, open, show "},{"id":"p24s3","text":"in folder, copy path |\n| 🔔 bell | Toggle auto-pop for new files |\n| `–` / `×` | Collapse to a floati"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"ng launcher button (with new-file badge) or hide |\n| Bottom \"open workspace folder\" | Opens the sess"},{"id":"p24s5","text":"ion's working directory |"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Panel state (open/collapsed) and the auto-pop preference persist in\n`localStorage`. The auto-pop bas"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"eline is per session: files that already\nexisted when the panel first saw the session do not re-trig"},{"id":"p25s3","text":" session: files that already\nexisted when the panel first saw the session do not re-trigger a popup."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"One npm package with two halves, registered as a single loader row\n(`cordis.patch.yml` → row `file-p"},{"id":"p27s2","text":" package with two halves, registered as a single loader row\n(`cordis.patch.yml` → row `file-panel`):"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The client half registers into the shipped `shell.overlay` slot (additive,\nframe-wide floating layer"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"), reads the current session through the standard\n`useSessions` prop, and polls the plugin's own loo"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"pback-only RPC channel.\nThe channel is registered with `ctx.connection.rpc.handle`, the sanctioned\ns"},{"id":"p29s4","text":"tatic-package RPC seam."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"### Security"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"- The `/file-panel` channel is registered with `authority: 'loopback'`, so\nonly pages served from `1"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"27.0.0.1` can call it. When the GUI is accessed\nover the network (`--trusted-host`), the panel shows"},{"id":"p31s3","text":" a notice and stays\ninactive.\n- Every read/reveal endpoint only accepts absolute paths that the trac"},{"id":"p31s4","text":"ker\nhas actually seen (a tool write or a watcher event under a watched working\ndirectory) — the RPC "},{"id":"p31s5","text":"can never be used as a generic file-read/reveal\nprimitive."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## Project layout"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"For a fast client-side iteration loop after changing `src/client.jsx`:"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"then hard-refresh the GUI page (`lib/client.js` is served with\n`cache-control: no-cache`; plugin *se"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"ts* only change on restart, but bundle\n*content* re-hashes per request — see `dsh-client-modules`). "},{"id":"p38s3","text":"During active\nUI development you can also run `pnpm run dev:web` from the harness checkout\nto rebuil"},{"id":"p38s4","text":"d client bundles on change."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"Built against the public seams of `@deepseek-ai/dsh` `0.1.0-rc.x`:"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"- host: `ctx.connection.rpc.handle` / `ctx.on('fs/observed')`\n- client: `shell.overlay` slot, `useSe"},{"id":"p41s2","text":"ssions` standard prop,\n`ctx.connection.rpc.call`, `ctx.locale`"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness is pre-release: those seams may move. If the panel stops\nworking after a `dsh` upgr"},{"id":"p42s2","text":"ade, check the pinned version in\n`package.json` and re-run the build."},{"id":"p43s1","text":"## Known limitations"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"- The recursive watcher uses `fs.watch({ recursive: true })` (Node ≥ 20).\nOn platforms where that is"},{"id":"p44s2","text":" unavailable, the panel still tracks everything\nthe harness `write`/`edit` tools produce, but shell-"},{"id":"p44s3","text":"side downloads may be\nmissed.\n- The panel is process-local: it starts empty after a restart (it only"},{"id":"p44s4","text":"\nrecords files it actually observed; it does not scan history).\n- `node_modules`, `.git`, and tempor"},{"id":"p44s5","text":"ary-file noise are ignored by design.\n- `reveal` on headless Linux reports `canReveal: false` and hi"},{"id":"p44s6","text":"des the\nbutton (no desktop to open)."},{"id":"p45s1","text":"## Publishing to GitHub / npm"},{"id":"p46s1","text":"1. Create a GitHub repo and push (the repo is already a git repository with\na `v0.1.4` tag):"},{"id":"p47s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p48s1","text":"2. Add the `dsh-plugin` topic on the\nrepo page (About → gear icon → Topics) together with\n`deepseek-"},{"id":"p48s2","text":"harness`, `dsh`, `deepseek`, and `file-preview`. The repo then\nappears on the public plugin topic pa"},{"id":"p48s3","text":"ge automatically.\n3. Users install with\n`dsh plugin --profile web add github:yu2025-luo/dsh-file-pan"},{"id":"p48s4","text":"el#v0.1.4`.\n4. Optionally publish to npm (`npm publish`) — then install with\n`dsh plugin --profile w"},{"id":"p48s5","text":"eb add dsh-file-panel`."},{"id":"p49s1","text":"Community catalogs that sync from the `dsh-plugin` topic:\nOh-My-DSH (auto-synced) and\nawesome-deepse"},{"id":"p49s2","text":"ek-harness\n(PR-based)."},{"id":"p50s1","text":"Remember to bump the version and re-run `npm run build` before releasing."},{"id":"p51s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p52s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
